", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/search?term=Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun", "search": true}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Bridget+St+John+I+Like+To+Be+With+You+In+The+Sun&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["“Before that, we had Bridget St. John. That was, I Like To Be With You In The Sun.”", "mentioned by the presenter but we couldn't work out when it played", "1960s/70s English folk singer on John Peel's Dandelion label; track features John Martyn on guitar, produced by John Peel, also appears on Dandelion/BBC compilations."]}], "counts": {"high": 6, "mid": 11, "low": 8}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:01:46", "end": "00:03:32", "text": "FBi Radio 94.5 FM Hello there. Big shout out to Peter Hollow for another great episode there. You're now tuned in to M5 and you are here with me, Wingnut, this evening. Jumping on again to the program to share some music with you. On this Sunday evening, we will play tunes for the next two hours, bridging the gap from Sunday to Monday. I am having some slight technical difficulties in the studio with some of the new CDJs that we have just acquired for DJs out there. You may or may not have been aware of some of the software updates that affect your playlists when you plug into the brand spanking new CDJ 3000 nexuses. But I'm currently suffering from that technical issue. So I've got a few things here and there. I've got a couple records. We'll see if we can get them playing. and we will just figure it out from there make sure that you keep it locked this is me wingnut on M5 hope you've had a good day hope you have a good evening let us know what you're up to if you are a late night listener tonight 0435123945 is the number give us a yell you're on FBI radio"}, {"start": "00:17:55", "end": "00:19:26", "text": "Hello there, listeners. You're tuned in to FBi Radio. You are here with me, Wingnut on M5. Some technical difficulties on my end tonight, trying to figure out how to work around it at the moment. Might be a bit of a touch-and-go show. this track underneath us a convenient long player coming in at 12 minutes long is Baby Food by Coil. Thankfully this track was exported onto my USB the list of hers. She must have had the updated record box software that goes with these new CDJs that I do not have so playing tracks off Darcy's USB basically shout out to you darcy good thing we have a similar taste in music before that we had brian eno with the big ship it's a teenage favorite of mine i always thought that it kind of sounded like it it the song kind of sounded like what it might"}, {"start": "00:19:32", "end": "00:19:54", "text": "Before that we had Sid Barrett from Pink Floyd fame. That track was Golden Hair. It's from his own solo project. And right off the top we had Roberto Muschi with Tamatave."}, {"start": "00:39:09", "end": "00:39:31", "text": "This track here, Agnes Obel, Stretch Your Eyes, it is the Quiet Village remix. Picked this up, digging for records in Japan a couple months ago. A little bit pitched down."}, {"start": "00:39:44", "end": "00:40:40", "text": "Just trying to make it work here on tonight's episode, having some technical difficulties in the studio, so we are having to think a little creatively. A couple long players, a couple pitch-down tracks. Going to get up to YouTube soon on the studio PCs and do a bit of YouTube DJing instead, I think. Shout out to my partner Darcy, whose music we've most have been playing so far. she managed to successfully export some of her playlists onto these USBs with the more recent Rekordboxes software that I do not have."}, {"start": "00:41:02", "end": "00:41:28", "text": "If you're wondering what you're listening to right now, other than the track, this is M5, and you are tuned in to FBi Radio. You're here with me. My name is Liam, aka Winger. Time is currently 11.41, so we've got an hour and 20 to go."}, {"start": "01:01:46", "end": "01:03:08", "text": "Hello there. The time is currently 12.01. We have clocked over from Sunday into Monday. So happy Monday for any listeners out there. You're currently listening to FBi Radio. The program is M5 and you're here with me, Wingnut. we are free how would you say we're a little bit off the cuff this evening having some technical difficulties in the studio so there's a bit of YouTube DJing going on it's kind of nice I'm enjoying it it's I'm going to sit down a little bit more rather than run between the decks and the studio desk that track just then was Anita Lane it was Lost in Music cover of that classic track by The Fall up next going to play something by Psychic TV the track is The Orchids hope that you are enjoying the program and make sure that you stay tuned for the next hour of M5 you are tuned in to FBI Radio"}, {"start": "01:16:27", "end": "01:17:49", "text": "Beautiful, beautiful track that one. It is, it was I Remember by Scott Seskind. That was off an old compilation put out on Efficient Space. From memory it was compiled by French DJ, DJ Sunday. He's got some good tunes, highly recommend checking him out. and the rest of the Efficient Space discography. Before that, we had a track by Orteca, a lesser-known mix of their track P.I.O.B. That was P.I.O.B. mix 2. Perfect midnight hours music, in my opinion. Quick shout-outs go to Ellie and the Ha tuned in for this YouTube DJ session. I hope you guys are enjoying the tunes current time is 12.17 shout out to all the late night hours tuning in on FM waves up next we've got another track this one is For the Love of You by Wayne and Glenn gonna roll with that nostalgic country tip for a little second"}, {"start": "01:27:16", "end": "01:29:06", "text": "Jack Adkins, American Sunset. It's from 1984. Some real strummy drum machine yearning there. Up next, we've got a bit of a personal classic. I feel like if you were listening to music on YouTube in 2015, 2016, this track was always kind of popping off in the recommendation algorithm it's called Baby by Donnie and Joe Emerson I'll play it in a moment but in the meantime just a reminder you are listening to M5 you're here with me Wingnut in the studio it's 12.30 so we've got about half an hour to go till we wrap things up But it's been a surprising and fruitful evening in the studio. I've had some troubles with the CDJs tonight. They were not loading my playlist, so I've just been playing tracks off my very large and long-standing YouTube playlist. I think I've probably had it since 2005. and 15, I'll probably do this in 16, currently clocking up to 4,218 tracks on it. So it's pretty mishmash, but I am enjoying digging back into some older stuff. Here is Baby by Donnie and Joe Emerson. Enjoy."}, {"start": "01:35:49", "end": "01:37:13", "text": "FBi Radio 94.5 Sydney with Lilly Grainger. Satsang with Mooji My Car I know my"}, {"start": "01:37:27", "end": "01:38:39", "text": "That track there was a lullaby song from the Solomon Islands. The track is called, or the artist is named Ro Ro Gwella. You might recognise the tune there. It was sampled in that track, Sweet Lullaby, which went on to be quite successful. but unfortunately, the original artist was not compensated for their contribution. Sad story, but a really beautiful song. Very touching stuff. Before that, we had Bridget St. John. That was, I Like To Be With You In The Sun. Alright, the time is 12.38. might try and inject a little bit more energy into the evening nothing crazy but a few less lullabies is what I'm thinking this track is Freighton Comp it's called Grinding"}, {"start": "01:47:20", "end": "01:47:41", "text": "It was Prins and Prins. The track was called Aisemkeit. Aisemkeit. This one underneath us. Single gun theory. It's open the skies. This is the extended mix."}, {"start": "01:51:47", "end": "01:52:22", "text": "Damn, what a tune. Love that one. Single Gun Theory. They've got some good songs. Highly recommended checking them out. They are an Aussie band. They were runners-up for Track of the Year, the same year that Itchy and Scratchy were up for an aria and won infamous aria awards that year."}, {"start": "01:58:55", "end": "01:59:30", "text": "We had some music I wasn't prepared to play and music that I haven't really listened to in quite a while, just off the dime, free associating here in the studio. Anyway, thanks to the special texters, Nahar and Ellie, for their tuning in today. This has been M5. You're listening to FBi Radio. Keep it locked. This track to close it out Is Always Then by the KVB Cheers and have a good evening Happy Monday"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:00"}, "track": {"title": "Ananau", "artists": [{"name": "Alborada"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:04:00"}, "track": {"title": "Tamatave", "artists": [{"name": "Roberto Musci & Giovanni Venosta"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:07:56"}, "track": {"title": "Golden Hair", "artists": [{"name": "Syd Barrett"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:09:53"}, "track": {"title": "The Big Ship", "artists": [{"name": "Brian Eno"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "high"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted"